  <section class="hwaet-project-content">

    <h2 class="hwaet-section-title">The Film</h2>

    <p class="hwaet-series-intro">
      In 1100, King William II is killed while hunting in the New Forest.
      His body is abandoned where it falls.
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>Drag Me to Winchester</em> follows Purkiss, the charcoal burner
      who discovers the dead king, as he attempts to carry the body through
      the forest to Winchester.
    </p>

  </section>


  <section class="hwaet-project-content hwaet-series-two">

    <h2 class="hwaet-section-title">The World</h2>

    <p>
      The journey passes through a medieval England shaped by Norman rule,
      older histories and competing beliefs. The landscape is inhabited
      not only by the living, but by the ghosts of those who came before them.
    </p>

  </section>


  <section class="hwaet-project-content hwaet-series-two">

    <h2 class="hwaet-section-title">Earthburn</h2>

    <p>
      The opening act of the feature has been adapted as
      <em>Earthburn</em>, a standalone HWAET short film centred on
      Purkiss's three-day charcoal burn in the New Forest.
    </p>

